# CVE Portal — Project Overview

## What it is
Internal PlainID tool that ingests Jira PLATFORM security tickets, enriches them with NVD CVE data, and creates/syncs PLAT "Security Vulnerability" tickets. Operators manage Customer SLAs and an allowed-image allowlist through an admin UI.

## Stack
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| API | FastAPI (Python 3.12), Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2 |
| Background | Celery + Redis |
| Database | PostgreSQL (external AWS RDS in prod; local `postgres` service in Docker) |
| Frontend | React 18 + TypeScript (Vite build) |
| Container | Single `portal` image: 2-stage Docker build (Node → React `dist/` baked into Python image) |

## Directory layout
```
api/
  app/
    main.py          # FastAPI app + all routes
    config.py        # Pydantic Settings (reads .env / env vars)
    models.py        # SQLAlchemy ORM models
    db.py            # engine + SessionLocal
    allowed_images.py  # image-name normalization helpers
    seed_allowed_images.py  # one-shot DB seed script
worker/
  app/
    celery_app.py    # Celery app
    tasks.py         # background processing tasks
ui/
  src/
    App.tsx          # entire frontend (single-file SPA)
    App.css
    api.ts           # typed API client + shared types
docker-compose.yml   # portal + worker + postgres + redis
api/Dockerfile       # 2-stage build (Node ui-build → python:3.12-slim)
```

## Environment variables (`.env`)
- `POSTGRES_DSN` — full connection string used by Python app (Pydantic Settings)
- `POSTGRES_HOST/USER/PASSWORD/DB/PORT` — used by `docker-compose.yml` to construct `POSTGRES_DSN` inside containers
- `REDIS_URL` — Redis connection string
- `JIRA_BASE_URL / JIRA_EMAIL / JIRA_API_TOKEN` — Jira REST API credentials

## Running locally
```bash
# Combined portal (API + UI) on :8080
docker compose build portal worker
docker compose up -d
# Seed allowed images on a fresh DB
docker compose exec portal python -m api.app.seed_allowed_images
```

The FastAPI app serves the React SPA via `StaticFiles(directory="dist", html=True)` mounted last, only when `dist/` exists (not in bare local dev).
